umbly is  accused of killing four people and  injuring seven others in a shooting at  oxford high school in november the teen  faces 24 charges of those charges you've  got four counts of first-degree murder  and one count of terrorism he's being  tried as an adult even though he was 15  at the time of the shooting before  allegedly opening fire on his classmates  teacher reported concerning behavior  from crumbly which including these  disturbing photos you're seeing of a gun  and a person bleeding other concerning  evidence show the teenager allegedly  killed animals and even stored the head  of a dead bird inside of a jar  crumbley's parents james and jennifer  are also charged in relation to the  shooting after allegedly disregarding  warning signs that their son was a  danger prosecutors also say they allowed  him easy access to the use of a gun  crumbly and his parents have pled not  guilty to all charges under michigan law  crumbly will now undergo a psychiatric  evaluation to determine whether he was  mentally ill or intellectually disabled  at the time of the shooting  melbourne an insanity defense it seemed  to be the obvious move here how does it  work and do you see it as a strong  defense in this case  i don't know if it's going to be a  strong defense in this case but  definitely it is a viable one so  basically the defense is going to say  listen we know we did it ethan you know  the defendant did in fact shoot these  people and take their lives however at  the time of the offense he did not  understand right from wrong he did not  understand that his actions were wrong  and could result in death so that is  what they're going to advance as their  theory they will have the drawings that  they can point to as well as some of the  other disturbing behaviors that he's  exhibited but the question is going to  be what were his actions right up until  and right after the incident and how can  that shape whether or not  what showing what his mental state was